Description: This package provides code to faciliate creation of the American
    Cancer Society Guideline Score. The Guideline Score is intended to be a
    compilation of lifestyle and behavioral factors associated with cancer risk.
    The score consists of 4 subcomponents - body mass index, physical activity,
    diet, and alcohol intake. Each component is derived and given a score with
    the sum of the scores being the overall ACS Guideline Score. The overall
    score has a range of 0-12 with higher scores indicating better overall diet
    quality, lower BMI, less alcohol consumption, and higher levels of physical
    activity.
